  "independent_publication_review": {
    "sha256": "1ba3d1fe540fc544f3e85c65710a10bde8a55209a78ae9184e17c8ed1c76af46",
    "text": "# Publication source review: complete frozen H25 GF(2)\n\n2026-10-28. **STATIC GO for one corrected publication-v2 full C correctness replay.** The first readonly publication attempt exposed a concrete cleanup defect, now repaired without changing the measured scientific driver, native engine or six performance samples. No remaining source blocker was found. This review supplies source clearance; it does not assert that the corrected run or hosted final-head checks have passed.\n\nReviewed package: `publication-repo/research/gf2-full-network/` under this round. Final reviewed `CODE-SOURCES.json` SHA-256 is `0ce6a3c120fc4f8f7ab98f044b3d7a72ce72310972c3846a4835bfc01e16a0d7`, covering 123 immutable files. Every listed file matched its digest in this static check. The publication-v2 stage has the identical manifest, driver and repaired wrapper. The driver remains `0d976d2eb6b845f20d4a3396591a806f966688b88693cd6a5f8a0c9e48925e36`, retaining the earlier source-review boundary.\n\n## Concrete failure and repair\n\nOriginal `verify_full.py:28` called `shutil.rmtree(temporary)` after successful verification. The full driver copies source directories with `copytree`; readonly export directories therefore retain mode 0555 inside the private runtime tree. Only the runtime root was made writable for the original certificate output. Unprivileged cleanup could not unlink files within the nested readonly engine directories.\n\nThe retained `runtime/runs/publication-full-readonly-C/` receipt confirms outer exit 1 after 33.381816457 seconds, unchanged source bytes/modes, and a `PermissionError` unlinking `finite_controls.py`. The inner scientific guard passed. This was a publication cleanup failure after scientific success, not a discarded timing sample or a changed theorem result. The package preserves the original wrapper as text plus receipt/stdout/stderr/usage and revision explanation in `evidence/publication-v1-failure/`.\n\nRepaired `verify_full.py`, SHA-256 `c65351d258bac75ae661298a351861452c81f990dd82768da819c1910cba8cd8`, changes only nonsymlink directories below its newly created private temporary root to 0755, after the replay's full scientific equality and source authentication checks. It then removes that private tree within the caught block. Immutable package/source directories are never chmodded; copied input file modes remain unchanged when verified. The corrected stage still has 0555 source directories and 0444 source files. This directly addresses the observed failure and justifies one fresh correctness validation, excluded from performance selection.\n\n## Wrappers, freshness and resource boundary\n\n`archive_support.py` authenticates every protected file, rejects symlinks and requires an exact Python/C code census. `CODE-SOURCES.json` itself is bound through committed package identity rather than an impossible self-hash. `VALIDATION.json` and optional publication status are explicitly mutable and never consulted as scientific PASS inputs.\n\n`replay.py` authenticates the guard from source, takes a nonblocking package-specific lock, requires a new output directory outside the repository and runs one B or C subprocess with no retry. It sets the guard's complete protected closure, timeout, aggregate allowance and 1-GiB sampled group RSS cap. The unchanged guard removes ambient Python-path/optimization settings and starts `/usr/bin/python3.12 -B` with external bytecode storage. Full entries reject optimized execution; the full driver additionally rejects already-loaded scientific modules and requires CPython 3.12. All scientific inputs and outputs are fresh private copies; no prior mutable result or PASS receipt replaces live work.\n\n`verify.py` launches the unchanged finite harness with a fresh external build/output directory. It preserves the requested normal or `-O` interpreter mode and checks the resulting mode. The finite controls use explicit checks rather than removable assertions. Both registered modes therefore exercise their controls anew; neither runs the full CLI with assertions disabled.\n\n`verify_full.py` requests one candidate replay with a 150-second inner guard. `VERIFY.json` gives it a 180-second outer timeout, leaving a nominal 30-second wrapper/cleanup margin. This is a bounded correctness check, not a promise of success on every host. The platform dependencies are disclosed. None of these wrappers requires Git or network access at execution time.\n\n## Input and output custody\n\n`SOURCES.json` contains exactly 42 input rows, all pinned to ancestor `7f9c2985de167e95d159040eee26fc03c1e27fb6`. Their paths equal the `VERIFY.json` input set and their hashes equal the retained `INPUT-COMMIT.json` inventory. No executable dependency requires unmerged PR5929 history. Commit ancestry/object verification remains the parent's publication check; I performed no Git operations.\n\n`check_artifacts.py` authenticates the six-payload transport manifest, bounds and streams decompression, and compares complete logical hashes against the immutable anchor. It checks full witness/rank byte counts, the typed-return structure, the literal reference certificate and complement receipt. Its typed validation supplements exact anchored bytes; it does not substitute a new numerical oracle. The README explicitly distinguishes the 55,839,507-byte observed complement stream from its stored digest/count/schema receipt. The large witness and rank artifacts retain their full logical bytes.\n\n## Claim and remaining publication work\n\nThe README/TASK/SOURCES/VERIFY boundary is appropriate: the fixed BCCBBC experiment measures the complete frozen historical H25 CLI **with retained exact observations**, cold copies/imports/custody/serialization, and every candidate's cold compile/link/load plus unchanged independent finite controls. Original full CLI assertions, real upstream verification, certificate and stdout remain executed through the unchanged driver. Publication wrappers add archive authentication overhead and their replays do not replace the measured driver samples.\n\nThe retained complete gate reports 27.843257% median wall and 28.094997% CPU reduction, passing the declared target and noise gates; slower C3 and both profile attempts remain visible. This review does not independently repeat those timings. The claim excludes bare-CLI, selected-frontier, PR5864 and kappa transfers. Predecessor credit and mathematical limitations are retained.\n\nThe parent must finish the already planned corrected readonly replay, commit/export metadata verification and exact-head hosted checks, then update mutable publication status from actual evidence. No new benchmark sequence, control requirement or mathematical work is requested. The earlier PR5864 goal remains separately blocked and paused streams remain paused.\n\nReviewer activity was limited to source/metadata reads, static inventories and hashes, retained receipt inspection, this report, and parent communication. No scientific module import, corpus decoding, compiler/numerical execution, Git/browser operation or delegation was performed.\n"
  },
